  "goodToKnow": "Das Grundrecht is a fundamental or basic right. The German Grundgesetz deliberately puts the Grundrechte first, in Articles 1 to 19, as a lesson from the Nazi era; Article 1 begins Die Würde des Menschen ist unantastbar (human dignity is inviolable). They include freedom of expression, religion and assembly. Anyone can file a Verfassungsbeschwerde (constitutional complaint) in Karlsruhe if they believe their Grundrechte have been violated."
